WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:08.260
Since 2014, a working group has been developing
proposals for the rehabilitation of the Kaiapoi River.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.960
Today we are at the corner of Charles and
Smith Street upstream of the Williams Street Bridge.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.520
So Neville tell me, what's happening with
this area of the river?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.640
Well this is where the corner many years ago
was realigned and it needs

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.680
to be meandered a bit more.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.660
So the channel will be dug out from up at
the Mafekin area. and come through here with

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.660
the main channel.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.500
And then batter of this corner you can see
behind us here, that will get battered off.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.150
And if these plantings that we have planted
as a trial all work and they all do what they

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:47.330
are supposed to do and grow, then that whole
area will go into the river with the plantings

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:52.470
to make sure that we: 1) Stabilise the bank,
but 2) That we can also help with purifying

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.380
water and things like that when we plant them.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.820
Putting all the plants back in here and making
sure that we have plantings that overhang

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.960
banks, meandering banks.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:11.260
Great collection point for eggs, for all species,
invertebrates, in which to play and make sure

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:16.680
that they breed in a proper manner and natural
manner within the river itself.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.840
So Neville, you mentioned sloping the bank
across the river here, what do you mean by that?

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.200
Well what it should do is create a much better
flow, a much more even flow.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.170
At the moment it comes around corner really
rapidly, causes erosion to the bank, the inner

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.050
bank here and that should just slow that a
little and stop some of the big eddies that

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.050
come around the corner.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:40.940
And just make a more consistent flow through
the river and a more naturalised bank on the other side.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.180
So how can people have their say?

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.000
Well, right here they can come in and there
will be an open day at Ruataniwha and people

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.240
can have their input that way.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.490
We have the website, we have councillors,
community board members and we really want

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.960
people to have their input.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:02.480
There are six proposals we'd like your feedback
on, attend our open day on the 27th of April

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.500
or find out more at waimakariri.govt.nz

